<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Val d'Aran</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aran Valley</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Val d'Aran is a valley in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>, in Catalonia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, lying on the northern side of the main ridge and drained by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garonne">Garonne</a>. Its people speak Aranese, a form of Occitan. Long disputed between the counts of Comminges and the Crown of Aragon, it has been part of Catalonia since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and enjoys special self-government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/val-daran.jpg" alt="Val d'Aran" width="320" height="105" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nickj · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pano_of_Boss%C3%B2st_in_Aran_Valley_in_Spain-cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
